gam Bandara, also called Pararajasinghe, was a son of King Vijayabahu VI of Kotte in Sri Lanka.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/raika-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Raika dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Raika dynasty ruled the kingdom of Doti in far-western Nepal in the late medieval and early modern periods.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raimbaut-d-orange"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raimbaut-d-orange.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raimbaut d'Orange</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raimbaut d'Orange was a Provençal troubadour and lord of part of the county of Orange.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rainier-iii-prince-of-monaco"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rainier-iii-prince-of-monaco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rainier III, Prince of Monaco</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rainier III was Prince of Monaco from 1949 to 2005, the longest reign in its history.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rainilaiarivony"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rainilaiarivony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rainilaiarivony</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rainilaiarivony was prime minister of the Merina kingdom of Madagascar from 1864 to 1895 and its real ruler.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rainulf-drengot"><span class="enc-name">Rainulf Drengot</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rainulf Drengot was a Norman mercenary leader in southern Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raipur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raipur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raipur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Raipur is a city in central India and the capital of the state of Chhattisgarh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/raiyoli"><span class="enc-name">Raiyoli</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Raiyoli is a village near Balasinor in Gujarat, India, known for one of the world's richest dinosaur fossil sites.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raj-darbhanga"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raj-darbhanga.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raj Darbhanga</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Raj Darbhanga was a great landholding estate in the Mithila region of northern Bihar, India, held by the Khandavala family of Maithil Brahmins.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raj-gond"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raj-gond.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raj Gond</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Raj Gonds are the ruling and landowning section of the Gond people of central India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raj-singh-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raj-singh-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raj Singh I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raj Singh I was Maharana of Mewar from 1652 to 1680.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/raja-ali-haji"><span class="enc-name">Raja Ali Haji</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raja Ali Haji was a Malay scholar, historian and poet of Bugis descent at the court of Riau-Lingga on the island of Penyengat.</span></a></li><li class="e