/encyclopedia/raja-kecil.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raja Kecil</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raja Kecil was a Minangkabau-backed adventurer who claimed to be the posthumous son of Sultan Mahmud Shah II of Johor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/raja-kuning"><span class="enc-name">Raja Kuning</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raja Kuning, 'the Yellow Queen', was the last of the four queens who ruled the Malay sultanate of Pattani in succession, reigning from 1635.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raja-melewar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raja-melewar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raja Melewar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raja Melewar was a prince of the Pagaruyung royal house of Minangkabau in Sumatra who was invited in 1773 by the chiefs of the Minangkabau settlements inland from…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/raja-rajeshwara-temple-vemulawada"><span class="enc-name">Raja Rajeshwara Temple, Vemulawada</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Raja Rajeshwara Temple at Vemulawada in Telangana, India, is a Shiva temple and one of the most visited pilgrimage centres of the state.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raja-ungu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raja-ungu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raja Ungu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raja Ungu, 'the Purple Queen', ruled the Malay sultanate of Pattani from 1624 to 1635, the third of four queens who governed it in succession.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajab"><span class="enc-name">Rajab</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span 